We add $\goldD{\dfrac{169}{16}}$ inside the parentheses, and subtract $\greenD{2}\cdot\goldD{\dfrac{169}{16}}$ outside them, to keep the expression equivalent.

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\greenD{2} \left(x^2 +\dfrac{13}{2} x\right) +20
\\\\
&=\greenD{2}\left(x^2 +\dfrac{13}{2} x+\goldD{\dfrac{169}{16}}\right) +20 -\greenD{2}\cdot\goldD{\dfrac{169}{16}}
\\\\
&=2 \left(x +\dfrac{13}{4}\right)^2 +20 -\dfrac{169}{8}
\\\\
&=2 \left(x +\dfrac{13}{4}\right)^2 -\dfrac{9}{8}
\end{align}$
